DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       sseettggiidd()  sets  the  effective group ID of the calling process.  If the
       calling process is privileged (more precisely: has the CCAAPP__SSEETTGGIIDD capa‐
       bility in its user namespace), the real GID and saved set‐group‐ID  are
       also set.

       Under  Linux,  sseettggiidd()  is implemented like the POSIX version with the
       __PPOOSSIIXX__SSAAVVEEDD__IIDDSS feature.  This allows a set‐group‐ID program  that  is
       not  set‐user‐ID‐root  to drop all of its group privileges, do some un‐
       privileged work, and then reengage the original effective group ID in a
       secure manner.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, zero is returned.  On error, -1 is returned, and  _e_r_r_n_o  is
       set to indicate the error.

EERRRROORRSS
       EEIINNVVAALL The  group  ID  specified in _g_i_d is not valid in this user name‐
              space.

       EEPPEERRMM  The calling  process  is  not  privileged  (does  not  have  the
              CCAAPP__SSEETTGGIIDD  capability  in its user namespace), and _g_i_d does not
              match the real group ID or saved  set‐group‐ID  of  the  calling
              process.

